1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,530
A hawker centre closes for repairs.

2
00:00:03,040 --> 00:00:04,330
The notice gives a date.

3
00:00:04,900 --> 00:00:08,980
A community coordinator still has to decide
where support is needed and what the budget

4
00:00:08,980 --> 00:00:13,090
can achieve. HawkerBridge turns that notice
into a reviewable decision.

5
00:00:13,620 --> 00:00:15,470
The project is owned by Shivam Gupta.

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,130
On September twenty eighth, seventeen centres
have scheduled closures.

7
00:00:24,660 --> 00:00:29,520
At an eight hundred metre threshold, six
subzones lose nearby hawker coverage at their

8
00:00:29,520 --> 00:00:34,420
representative points. Those areas contain
about ninety one thousand Census twenty

9
00:00:34,420 --> 00:00:38,800
twenty residents. That is a screen for
investigation, not a count of people going

10
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:42,730
hungry. Walking barriers and other food options
still need checking.

11
00:00:43,300 --> 00:00:46,860
A coordinator can compare a cleaning date
change before funding support.

12
00:00:46,860 --> 00:00:49,570
The official schedule stays unchanged.

13
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:59,640
Now consider five percent participation, four
dollars per meal, three hundred dollars

14
00:00:59,640 --> 00:01:03,720
to set up each collection locality, and
capacity of a hundred and fifty meals per

15
00:01:03,720 --> 00:01:08,420
locality. With fifteen hundred dollars, the
planner allocates two hundred and twenty

16
00:01:08,420 --> 00:01:11,010
five meals across two proposed localities.

17
00:01:11,900 --> 00:01:15,050
These locations and capacities still need an
operator's verification.

18
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:27,550
At three thousand dollars, planned capacity
reaches four hundred and fifty meals.

19
00:01:28,440 --> 00:01:30,870
Double the budget to six thousand, and it stays
there.

20
00:01:31,740 --> 00:01:35,030
Three localities times a hundred and fifty
meals is the ceiling.

21
00:01:35,880 --> 00:01:38,370
Proposed spending is twenty seven hundred
dollars.

22
00:01:39,120 --> 00:01:40,590
That is the useful decision.

23
00:01:41,660 --> 00:01:44,890
Verify more capacity before seeking more
funding for this arrangement.

24
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:58,130
Save the proposal with its assumptions and
source evidence.

25
00:01:58,940 --> 00:02:02,530
Inspect the local review checklist, then export
a coordination brief.

26
00:02:03,320 --> 00:02:05,490
Nothing here books a venue or dispatches food.

27
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:18,450
Behind the interface, Databricks preserves the
source data in governed tables,

28
00:02:19,180 --> 00:02:23,670
quarantines ambiguous dates, and records nine
scenario comparisons in MLflow.

29
00:02:23,860 --> 00:02:28,910
This public application runs through Firebase
and uses that verified data publication.

30
00:02:29,540 --> 00:02:32,930
The results are modelled decisions, not
measured social impact.

31
00:02:32,960 --> 00:02:36,350
The next test is one operator and one scheduled
closure.

32
00:02:37,060 --> 00:02:41,520
Measure preparation time, verify every proposed
venue, and learn whether the workflow

33
00:02:41,520 --> 00:02:47,090
earns repeat use. HawkerBridge makes that
decision visible, testable and reviewable.
